# Copy this to demo/.env and fill in real values. run.sh sources .env
# automatically (if present) and forwards these onto its `vagrant ssh`
# commands — see ai_env_argv in run.sh. .env itself is gitignored; this
# example file is the only one that's ever committed.
#
# This file is sourced as shell, not parsed as plain KEY=value pairs, so
# quote a value if it contains a space or a shell-special character
# ($, `, ", \) — e.g. HOSTVEIL_OPENAI_API_KEY="sk-...". A real API key is
# ordinarily plain alphanumeric/hyphens and needs none of this.
#
# Nothing here is required. With no .env, or one that sets none of these,
# `./run.sh scan` / `./run.sh web` behave exactly as they do without AI —
# `--ai` and the dashboard's "Explain with AI" just report the provider
# unreachable, the same as everywhere else in hostveil.
#
# Uncomment ONE provider block below. See https://hostveil.seolcu.com/docs/ai
# for the full contract (what --ai sends, and what it never does).

# ── OpenCode Zen / OpenCode Go (OpenAI-compatible gateways) ────────────────
# HOSTVEIL_AI_PROVIDER=openai
# HOSTVEIL_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1   # or .../zen/go/v1 for Go
# HOSTVEIL_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# HOSTVEIL_OPENAI_MODEL=                                 # a model ID from that provider's own catalog

# ── Any other OpenAI-compatible vendor (OpenRouter, Groq, Together, …) ─────
# HOSTVEIL_AI_PROVIDER=openai
# HOSTVEIL_OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# HOSTVEIL_OPENAI_API_KEY=
# HOSTVEIL_OPENAI_MODEL=

# ── Anthropic ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOSTVEIL_AI_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# HOSTVEIL_ANTHROPIC_MODEL=                              # default: claude-opus-5

# ── Local Ollama, reached from inside the VM (rarely what you want here) ──
# HOSTVEIL_AI_PROVIDER=ollama
# HOSTVEIL_OLLAMA_HOST=
# HOSTVEIL_OLLAMA_MODEL=
